      "analytic_result": "H=Tr[C(C-(Tr C)/r I)^2] is polynomial, zero with zero occupied source on rank-r coherent current. For a prepared two-ray current it is exactly r(rho+sigma)rho sigma(1-s^k), and a fixed-trace partner split costs 2rho^3 epsilon^2. H is nonnegative for C>=0 but sign-indefinite for general Hermitian C. The linear trace mass term and cubic H carry distinct coefficients unless an origin fixes their relative scale.",
      "smooth_nonnegative_boundary": "H4=Tr[C^2(C-(Tr C)/r I)^2] is nonnegative for every Hermitian C and is exactly 2r(rho sigma)^2(1-s^k)^2 on a prepared pair. More generally, if a smooth globally nonnegative correction vanishes on every coherent rank-r current, its gradient and Hessian along tangent coherent-ray rotations vanish there. A prepared pair has the same first-order tangent, so its angular excess is o(theta^2). A positive quadratic pair stiffness in this construction requires a correction that is sign-indefinite off the positive-current cone or a different coherent self law.",
      "scope": "Matrix-current algebra and complete noncommuting differential; no full spatial solution, collision, or cross-depth embedding."
